�����"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|15|STARRED   |36", "t": "Restoration of Temples in Tamil Nadu", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO-36\nANSWERED ON- 02/02/2024\nOFFLINE SUBMISSION OF APPLICATIONS\n36.  SHRI MARGANI BHARAT\n  SHRIMATI CHINTA ANURADHA\nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be please to state :-\n(a)  Whether  the  Ministry  only  allows  for  offline  submission  of\napplications for some positions that it is recruiting for;\n(b) if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor;\n(c) The details of the rules governing the procedure for shortlisting or\nselection of candidates applying to the position of consultants at the\nunder-secretary level in the Ministry;\n(d) Whether the Ministry declares the list of shortlisted candidates for\neach post it is conducting recruitment for;\n(e) if  so, the details of  the processes it follows for transparency in\nrecruitment, and if not, the reasons therefor; and\n(f)  the  reasons  for  not  publishing  the  list  of  Consultants  finally\nappointed to the advertised posts in recent times?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS\n(SHRI V. MURALEEDHARAN)\n(a to f) Applications for engagement of consultants in the Ministry are\ninvited  through  open  advertisement  published  on  the  Ministry’s\nwebsite. These applications are accepted through online (email) as\nwell as offline mode. Eligible applicants are shortlisted on the basis of\ncriteria indicated in the advertisement. The shortlisted candidates are\ninterviewed by a Selection Committee appointed by the Competent\nAuthority in the Ministry. Names of the Consultants who are engaged\nin the Ministry are available on the Ministry’s website.\n*****"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|15|STARRED   |37", "t": "Establishment of KVs/JNVs", "head": "������������������� �\n��������������������������������������� �\n��\n��������� �\n������������������������ �\n���������������������������� �