the details thereof; \n(b) whether the participants from 928 locations joined the launch event virtually and if so, the \ndetails thereof; \n(c) whether the upgradation and modernization of more than 1000 schools under PM SHRI in \nUttar Pradesh has already been completed and if so, the details thereof; \n(d) whether 1753 schools have been selected to be upgraded as PM SHRI schools in Uttar \nPradesh and if so, the details thereof; and \n(e) the other steps being taken by the Government for improvements in school infrastructure \nsuch as smart classrooms, science laboratories, digital libraries an d sports facilities, resulting \nin the development of integrated campuses for providing holistic school education? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EDUCATION \n(SMT. ANNPURNA DEVI) \n \n(a) to (e): The Cabinet has approved a Centrally Sponsored Scheme named Pradhan Mantri \nSchools for Rising India (PM SHRI) on 7th September, 2022. These schools are to showcase \nthe implementation of the National Education Policy 2020 and emerge as exemplar schools \nover a period of time, and also offer leadership to other schools in the neighbourhood. Under \nthe PM SHRI scheme, in first phase of selection, a total of 6207 schools have been selected \nfrom 29 States/UTs/KVS/NVS including 928 Schools against a total of 1753 Schools, in the \nstate of Uttar Pradesh. Further the process of selection of schools for the second phase of the \nPM SHRI scheme is under process. \nThe Government of Uttar Pradesh organized launch of PM SHRI Scheme in the state on 4th \nJanuary, 2024.  Principals, Head Teachers, and Teachers from the 220 PM SHRI schools \n\nphysically attended the launch event in Lucknow. The representatives of remaining PM SHRI \nschools participated virtually through various online platforms. \nThe PM -SHRI schools envisage incorporating environment friendly aspects like Energy \nefficient using solar panels and LED lightings, nutrition gardens with natural farming, waste \nmanagement, plastic free, water conservation and harvesting, study of traditions/practises \nrelated to protection of environment, climate change related hackathons, encouragement of \nusage of environment-friendly modes of transport and awareness generation to incorporate \norganic lifestyle. PM -SHRI schools are also promoting Early Childhood Care through \nBalvatika, regular health check-ups especially for 100% immunization, play-based learning, \nparent education programs to enhance parenting skills, age -appropriate toys and activities, \nexposure to books and storytelling. Further, digital pedagogy in PM -SHRI schools, are \npromoted through ICT and digital initiatives. This includes providing digital libraries with \ntablets containing pre -loaded educational content, Classroom Digital Boards, Smart \nClassrooms, Digital Content Creation, and technological interventions to support  teachers \nand address language barriers. \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|15|UNSTARRED |271", "t": "RUSA Funding to Educational Institutions in Ernakulam, Kerala", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 271 \nANSWERED ON 05.02.2024 \n \nRUSA FUNDING TO EDUCATIONAL INSTITUTIONS IN ERNAKULAM, KERALA \n \n271. SHRI HIBI EDEN: \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state:  \n(a) whether the Rashtriya Uchchatar Shiksha  Abhiyan (RUSA) has provided funding to educational  \ninstitutions in Ernakulam district, Kerala and if so,  the details including the list, name of colleges, \nlocation, amount for the financial years 2019-20, 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23 and 2023-24; \n(b) whether the Government has any plans to  increase the allocation of RUSA funding to educational  \ninstitutions in Ernakulam district, Kerala, if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; and \n(c) whether the Government has taken any steps  to ensure that RUSA funding is being utilized  \neffectively and efficien tly by educational institutions in Ernakulam district, if so, the details thereof \nand if not, the reasons therefor? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EDUCATION \n(Dr. SUBHAS SARKAR) \n \n(a): The details of the funds released under Rashtriya Uchchatar Shiksha Abhiyan ( RUSA) for the \ninstitutions approved in Ernakulam district of Kerala including the list, name of colleges, location,  \namount for the financial years 2019 -20, 2020 -21, 2021-22 and  2022-23 is given at \nhttps://www.education.gov.in/sites/upload_files/mhrd/files/upload_document/Enrakulam_Releases.pdf. \nNo funds have been released to Kerala in 2023-24 as on date.  \n \n(b): The government has recently approved the third phase of RUSA in the form of Pradhan Mantri \nUchchatar Shiksha Abhiyan (PM-USHA) with an outlay of Rs. 12926.10 crore for the period 2023-24 to \n2025-26 to cater to needs of educationally unserved/underserved areas. Fund release under PM-USHA is \ndependent upon the submission of proposals by States/UTs subject to the guidelines of the scheme.  \n \n(c): Since the scheme of RUSA is a Centrally Sponsored Scheme  and the beneficiary institutions are \nState government or Government -aided institutions , state government is primarily responsible for the \nimplementation of the scheme within the State . However, the Central Government also regularly \nmonitors the implementation of the scheme through review meetings with the State Government. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|15|UNSTARRED |272", "t": "Quality Education to Children of Educationally Backward Districts", "head": " GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 272 \nANSWERED ON 05.02.2024 \n \nQUALITY EDUCATION TO CHILDREN OF EDUCATIONALLY BACKWARD DISTRICTS \n \n272. SHRI SUSHIL KUMAR RINKU:  \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state:  \n(a) whether the Government has the data of educationally backward districts of the country; \n(b) if so, the details thereof including Punjab; \n(c) the details of awareness programmes being formulated by th e Government to facilitate children of \nthese backward districts to get quality education in their surrounding areas; and \n(d) the details of the funds estimated for the purpose and the time by which these are likely to be \nimplemented? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EDUCATION \n(Dr. SUBHAS SARKAR) \n \n(a) to ( d) The government has launched the third phase of Rashtriya Uchchatar Shiksha Abhiyan \n(RUSA) in June 2023 in the form of Pradhan Mantri Uchchatar Shiksha Abhiyan  (PM-USHA) with an \noutlay of Rs. 12926.10 crore for the period 2023 -24 to 2025 -26 to cater to needs of educationally \nunserved/underserved areas. Under PM -USHA, priority is given to Focus Districts. The focus districts \nare identified by the concerned States /UTs based on various criteria including low Gross Enrollment \nRatio, the proportion of disadvantaged categories such as Scheduled Castes, Scheduled Tribes,  etc. The \ndetails of the Focus Districts identified and submitted by the States/UTs , including Punjab, as on date is \ngiven at Annexure. The scheme envisages improvement in access, equity and excellence in State Higher \nEducation system through support under various components viz., Multi-Disciplinary Education and \nResearch Universities (MERU), Grants to Strengthen Universities, Grants to Strengthen Colleges, New \nModel Degree Colleges and Gender Inclusion and Equity Initiatives.  \n \n \n***** \n  \n\nANNEXURE \nANNEXURE REFERRE D TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (A) TO (D ) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 272 ANSWERED ON 05.02.2024 ASKED BY SHRI SUSHIL \nKUMAR RINKU , HON’BLE MEMBER OF PARLIAMENT REGARDING QUALITY \nEDUCATION TO CHILDREN OF EDUCATIONALLY BACKWARD DISTRICTS \nList of Focus Districts identified by States/UTs under PM-USHA \nState \nNo. of \nFocus \nDistricts \nName Of Focus Districts \nAndaman A