 of number of new highways proposed to be \nconstructed in the country and the Budgetary allocations proposed \nin this regard, State-wise? \n  \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n(a) and (b)       The Ministry keeps on receiving proposals from various \nState Governments / Union Territories (UTs), including State \nGovernment of Uttar Pradesh, for declaration / upgradation of State \n\nRoads, including State Highways (SHs), as new National Highways \n(NHs). The Ministry considers declaration of some State Roads, \nincluding SHs, as NHs from time to time based on the fulfillment of \nthe criteria for declaration of NHs, requirement of connectivity, inter-\nse priority and availability of funds. \n            About 14 numbers of state roads including SHs and greenfield \nalignment in 923 km length were notified as new NHs in the State of \nUttar Pradesh during last five years (FY 2018-19 to 2022-23). \n            About 3,959 km length of NHs, including n ewly notified NHs, \nwere developed/ constructed in the State of Uttar Pradesh during last \nfive years and the total expenditure incurred was about Rs. 83,755 \ncrore. \n(c)        Development and maintenance of NHs, including newly \nnotified NHs, is a continuous process and works are accordingly \ntaken up to keep the NHs in traffic worthy conditions depending upon \ninter-se priority, traffic density and availability of funds. \nState / UT – wise details of targets for development / \nconstruction of NHs, including newly  notified NHs, during 2023 -24 \nand achievements upto December, 2023 are at Annexure-I.   \nState / UT / Agency – wise details of expenditure on NH works, \nincluding newly notified NHs, during 2023 -24 (upto December, 2023) \nare at Annexure-II.            \n  \n  \n  \n\nANNEXURE-I \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (c) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 986 ANSWERED ON 08.02.2024 ASKED \nBY SHRI MALOOK NAGAR REGARDING HIGHWAYS IN UTTAR \nPRADESH   \nState / UT – wise details of targets for development / construction of \nNHs, including newly notified NHs, during 2023-24 and achievements \nupto December, 2023:   \nSr. No. State /UT  Target FY-2023-24  \n(in Km) \nAchievement \n(in Km) \n1 Andhra Pradesh 728 375 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 351 192 \n3 Assam 527 106 \n4 Bihar 697 198 \n5 Chhattisgarh 252 161 \n6 Dadra and Nagar Haveli And Daman \nand Diu 0 0 \n8 Goa 11 7 \n9 Gujarat 571 224 \n10 Haryana 314 144 \n11 Himachal Pradesh 225 125 \n12 Jammu & Kashmir 269 129 \n13 Jharkhand 258 117 \n14 Karnataka 823 372 \n15 Kerala 259 44 \n16 Madhya Pradesh 676 346 \n17 Maharashtra 1866 854 \n18 Manipur 399 59 \n19 Meghalaya 239 58 \n20 Mizoram 298 96 \n21 Nagaland 233 57 \n22 Odisha 377 129 \n23 Puducherry 0 0 \n\n24 Punjab 386 158 \n25 Rajasthan 749 550 \n26 Sikkim 170 37 \n27 Tamil Nadu 728 476 \n28 Telangana 496 289 \n29 Tripura 118 29 \n30 Uttar Pradesh 1120 541 \n31 Uttarakhand 284 105 \n32 West Bengal 181 134 \n33 Delhi 35 20 \n34 Andaman & Nicobar Islands 16 6 \n35 Ladakh 157 76 \nGrand Total 13,814 6,216 \n  \n  \n  \n  \n  \n\n  \nANNEXURE-II \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (c) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 986 ANSWERED ON 08.02.2024 ASKED \nBY SHRI MALOOK NAGAR REGARDING HIGHWAYS IN UTTAR \nPRADESH  \nState / UT / Agency – wise details of expenditure on NH works, \nincluding newly notified NHs, during 2023-24 (upto December, 2023): \nExpenditure for development of NHs is incurred by different agencies, \ne.g. NHAI, NHIDCL, BRO, NHLML and State/UT Governments. \nFor works being executed through State Governments, details of \nfunds allocated and expenditure incurred / funds released for \ndevelopment of NHs during current year 2023 -24 (upto December, \n2023):- \nAmount in Rs. Crore \nSl. No. State/UT 2023-24 (Till 31.12.2023) \nAllocation Expenditure  \n1 Andhra Pradesh 3,208 2,510 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 520 520 \n3 Assam 350 266 \n4 Bihar 2,193 1,332 \n5 Chhattisgarh 1,018 938 \n6 